      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-10-12_WidnesExaminer_art0016" n="art0016">
        <head>HAVE YOU LIVER-CHILL. The Peril of Autumn Ailments. KER-NAK A CURE AND A PROTECTION.</head>
        <p>HAVE YOU LIVER-CHILL. The Peril of Autumn Ailments. KER-NAK A CURE AND A PROTECTION.</p>
        <p>The most trying time of the year even for robust people, let alone the weakly, is undoubtedly about now when the Autumn days get dark and cold. Mild afternoons tempt people to go without sufficient clothing, and a moment after sundown they find themselves struck with the cold of early night. A chill on the liver or kidneys is a dangerous condition that may arrive in This way or in con- sequence of one being forced to wear wet clothing after being caught in cold showers. Chronic colds, influenza, and back pains and rheumatism also are largely due to the weather. Consumption is often contracted through unex- pected change in the weather weakening the lungs. The ancient Egyptians, whose climate, though very different from ours, was equally treacherous, found their best health preservation in the medi- cines they made from the most precious portions of fruit. Twentieth century scientists have equally, realised the wisdom of seeking out Nature's remedies for Nature's ills, and in Ker- Nak we have the ideal cure for Autumn sickness and the effects of chill. The stomach and liver have to play the rOle of the engine furnaces, and transform our food into heat-units and good bone and blood. One of the first results of the liver and stomach being defective, and unable to keep up the bodily fire in this way, is to increase our liability to colds and chills. You have that familiar chilly feeling, sharp pains in the back, feel below par and so off your food. Many red noses, chilblains, and shiverino's might be scr explained ; not to mention influenza, typhoid fever, and other serious epidemic diseases, which gain an entrance into many people's systems,through the bodily beat having been allowed to" smoulder "in this way. A course of Ker-Nak quickly ends "liver chill," drives out that "chilly feeling," puts an end to th( se unpleasant shivers, and soothes and restores the digestive apparatus as no ordinary mineral drugs ever were able to do. Directly any of these symptoms appear, commence to take Ker-Nak without delay. Nature, in the guise of Ker-Nak, is to the body what a clever stoker or engineer is to a faulty furnace. The bodily fire or vitality is kept up; and all those perilous "cold weather ailments"— lung-chill, kidney-chill, pneumonia, and influenza are kept out. Ker-Nak is the Natural remedy of unequalled excellence for all Autumn ailments, constipation, piles, indigestion, stomach-ache, pains in the back and under the shoulder-blades, vomiting, loss of appetite, feebleness or gout and old-age, anwmia and female ailments, liver troubles, and all ail- ments arising from a disordered stomach. Of all chemists, in cases, is. and 2s. 9d., or direct from Ker-Nak Natural ltemedy, Ltd., Turnmill- slreet, London.</p>
