      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-10-12_WidnesExaminer_art0111" n="art0111">
        <head>COMING DENOMINATIONAL GATHERINGS.</head>
        <p>COMING DENOMINATIONAL GATHERINGS.</p>
        <p>After the Baptist meetings—now in session ----tke assembly of the Congregational Union will 'claim attention. The meetings are to be held from October 13 to 18, under the presidency of Mr. J. Compton Rickett, M.P., at Blackpool. Among the subjects that are being dealt with is 'The Deepening of the Spiritual Life," which Dr. Horton and Rev. J. H. Jowett, M.A., are to speak to. There is to be a theological conference on Wednes- day, when "The Relation between Theology and the Spiritual Life" will be discussed, and on the following day a more or less kin- dred subject, "Social Interests and the Spiritual Life of the Church," forms the topic of conference, to be opened by the Rev. F. W. Newland, M.A., of the Claremont Mission. On Wednesday also there is to be a conference on the subject of the "Free Churches and the Land," at which addresses will be given by Dr. Paton, the well-known philanthropist, and Mr. Frederick Horne, the brother of the Rev. C. Silvester Horne, and a Parliamentary candidate in the last election. E. J. M.</p>
        <p>COMMERCIAL Fan.rtrtEs.—According to " Kemp'r Mercantile Gazette," the total tutnber of commercial failures recorded in England and Wales during the week ending Friday, October 4th,was 148, viz. :—New bankruptcy proceedings pubdsbed in the " London Gazette," 81; deeds of arrangement registered, 64. The respective numbers in the corresponding seek of last year were : Bankruptcies, 91; deeds of arrangement, 89— total 180 ; being a decrease of 32. The total num- ber of commeicial failures recorded during the 40 weeks of the present :tear is :5,882 ; the total number recorded in the corresponding 40 weeks of last year was 6,421, showing a deer,ase of 539.</p>
