      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-10-12_WidnesExaminer_art0127" n="art0127">
        <head>NOTES ON GAMES AND ATHLETICS.</head>
        <p>NOTES ON GAMES AND ATHLETICS.</p>
        <p>RUGBY FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>By " Ovallst."</p>
        <p>My special description of, and comments on the New Zealanders' opening match at Bramley on Wednesday, will be found in another column.</p>
        <p>Oldham have twice had the good fortune in recent matches to visit Warrington and find the local team handicapped by absentees. Last year they won with ease in both League matches, but Warrington had ample compensation in beating Oldham in both the Lancashire and Northern Union Cup Competitions. This season they have made a bad start against their old foes for the Oldham men came to Warrington on Saturday and beat the locals by 10 points to 7 points, I have not much hope that Warrington will equalise matters when they go to Watersheddings, for they have only won once there in the course of their history. Oldham have certainly a fine record against Warrington and one of their officials informs me that Warrington have only beaten them five times at Warrington in the last 16 years. It is a fact that the Oldham men say they would rather meet Warrington at Warrington than most clubs on neutral ground.</p>
        <p>On Saturday Warrington had to take the field without Fish, Brooks, and Taylor, probably the three best backs the club possesses, while Oldham had only one absentee from their rear division. Still, there was plenty of confidence in the home team, but somehow they failed to rise to the occasion and never gave a glimpse of first-class form. Oldham were much superior in the first half, and when later on Warring- ton were handicapped by the loss of Tilley they seemed unable to take advantage of their opportunities. War- rington got the only try in the second half, and there is a possibility that with Tilley in his place they might have won. Truth to tell, however, the honours went to the better side on Saturday.</p>
        <p>-*-</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-10-12_WidnesExaminer_art0128" n="art0128">
        <gap reason="ocrQuality" quantity="2" unit="words">
